{
  "about": "Location classes of the house ledger (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.4, 6.5, 6.11; WP1). An entity belongs to a class when its type, one of its is_a names or its category is listed under the class (types / is_a / categories), or, for 'fields', when the named field is truthy (or equals the listed value). A location chain (an entity's location, its container's, ...) is in a class when any link is. Domains extend these lists in their WP-D packages by adding names here through the kernel owner. waste: waste containers (accepting sinks by waste_stream; a waste_stream on an item only names the stream it belongs to, so it never makes the item a waste location: the kernel's is_waste_container rule); drain: drains and the drain relation; basin: sinks and tubs (not a loss unless the relation is drain); vacuum: vacuum bins; compost; outdoor_waste: curb carts and the pickup zones (curb, street; not the driveway); carrier: tools and vessels that carry mess (a listed transit instance only); absorbent: towels, cloths, sponges, granules (mess soaked into them is 'elsewhere'); food_contact: food and drink vessels and food stores (rho 0, a wrong sink for every dirty class); pet_bowl; plant: plants and their pots (a wrong sink for dirty liquids); bed_textile: beds and textile stores; concealing: rugs and mats (relation under: hidden); hazardous_waste: the hazardous-waste stream; toilet, utility_sink, floor_drain: the dirty-water sinks; grease_container. hazard_created: entity types that, created by the robot, must end in an accepting sink for their class ('sinks': location classes or waste streams that accept them).",
